  "notes": "Emberpup, a red fox-puppy with a cream muzzle and chest and a flame at the tip of its tail, drawn in the style of the monsters that walk around in GBA monster games: dark closed outline, 3 shades lit from the top-left, eyes with a glint. Seen from the front (down), the back (up) and the side (facing right; mirrored for left). Each view has a standing frame, a breathing frame (1 px lower), a blink, the frames it steps (back or left foot up, passing pose 1 px higher, other foot up, passing pose) with, and an attack lunge. Every frame stays inside the 16x16 box with its outline closed, so nothing is ever cut at the edges. Too many frames to keep whole in video memory: it streams (only the frames on screen are loaded).",
